{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>He</b> — reveals deep and hidden things that no man can know, when His servants such as these pray to Him, for He revealed to me the secret of the dream." "<b>Knows what is in the darkness</b> — the opposite of man. And in my opinion the sense is: what is in the power to be, like <i>and He brings out light from darkness</i>." "And the sense of <b>and light dwells with Him</b> — all is before Him as though done." "And the word <b>dwells</b> [שרא] — like <i>encamps</i>." "<b>And light</b> [נהורא] — like <i>and let no brightness shine upon him</i>, and similarly <i>the tunnels</i>."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:25.578968340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}